  "notes": "West leads the ♥K against 3♠. West wins the trick, continues with the ♥A, and gives East a heart ruff. East switches to clubs, won by South. South should begin by testing trump. A spade to the ♠K reveals a certain trump loser when East discards.\n\nSouth must hope that the diamond finesse is winning. There still exists what looks like a certain club loser. The only chance is to hope that West began with less than 3 clubs. It will then be possible to endplay him with his trump trick.\n\nA spade is played to the ♠A. South next takes the diamond finesse, cashes dummy's top diamond, and leads a third diamond, ruffing. South then cashes his other club winner and exits in trump.\n\nWest wins this trick, but hopefully he has no more clubs to play. West's forced heart return yields a ruff and discard.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
